==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɹæbəl/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-rabble.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|æbəl|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|rablen||to ramble; rave; speak in a confused manner}}, cognate with {{cog|dum|rabbelen||to talk; chatter; trifle}}, {{cog|de|rabbeln}}, {{m|de|robbeln||to chatter; prattle}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|ravel}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb|rabbl|ing}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[speak]] in a [[confused]] manner; talk [[incoherently]]; [[utter]] [[nonsense]]
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To speak confusedly or incoherently; [[gabble]] or [[chatter]] out

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|rabel}}, probably from the verb (see above).

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[mob]]; a [[disorderly]] crowd.
# The mass of [[common]] people; the lowest [[class]] of [[people]].

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|en|plebs}}
* {{l|en|riffraff}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|en|rabble rouser}}
* {{l|en|rabblesome}}

